# Testing Conventions

## API Tests (Vitest + Supertest)

Place test files next to the source file:

```
apps/api/src/nvm/
├── nvm.parser.ts
├── nvm.parser.spec.ts   ← unit test
├── nvm.service.ts
└── nvm.service.spec.ts  ← unit test (with mocks)
apps/api/src/routes/
└── nvm.routes.spec.ts   ← integration test with Supertest
```

Unit test pattern:

```typescript
// nvm.parser.spec.ts
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { parseInstalledVersions } from './nvm.parser.js';

describe('parseInstalledVersions', () => {
  it('identifies the active version', () => {
    const stdout = '->     v22.11.0 (default)\n       v20.5.0';
    const result = parseInstalledVersions(stdout);
    expect(result).toHaveLength(2);
    expect(result[0].active).toBe(true);
    expect(result[0].default).toBe(true);
    expect(result[0].version).toBe('22.11.0');
  });

  it('returns an empty array for empty input', () => {
    expect(parseInstalledVersions('')).toEqual([]);
  });
});
```

Integration test with Supertest:

```typescript
// nvm.routes.spec.ts
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';
import request from 'supertest';
import app from '../../server.js';
import * as nvmService from '../nvm/nvm.service.js';

vi.mock('../nvm/nvm.service.js');

describe('POST /api/versions/install', () => {
  it('rejects an invalid version with 400', async () => {
    const res = await request(app).post('/api/versions/install').send({ version: '../etc/passwd' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(400);
  });

  it('returns 200 for a valid version', async () => {
    vi.mocked(nvmService.install).mockResolvedValue({ stdout: 'ok', stderr: '' });
    const res = await request(app).post('/api/versions/install').send({ version: '22' });
    expect(res.status).toBe(200);
  });
});
```

## Angular Tests (Vitest + @testing-library/angular)

```typescript
// version-card.component.spec.ts
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/angular';
import { VersionCardComponent } from './version-card.component';

describe('VersionCardComponent', () => {
  it('disables buttons while isLoading', async () => {
    const { fixture } = await render(VersionCardComponent);
    const comp = fixture.componentInstance;
    comp.isLoading.set(true);
    fixture.detectChanges();
    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /install/i })).toBeDisabled();
  });
});
```

## Vitest Configuration (API – `vitest.config.ts`)

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    globals: true,
    environment: 'node',
    include: ['src/**/*.spec.ts'],
    coverage: {
      provider: 'v8',
      reporter: ['text', 'lcov'],
      include: ['src/**/*.ts'],
      exclude: ['src/**/*.spec.ts'],
      thresholds: { lines: 70, functions: 70 },
    },
  },
});
```

## Playwright E2E (`apps/e2e/`)

```typescript
// install-flow.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('can install a Node.js version', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('http://localhost:4200');
  await expect(page.getByText('nvm Manager')).toBeVisible();
  await page.getByLabel('Version').fill('22');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Install' }).click();
  await expect(page.getByText(/Installing/)).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Naming Rules

- Test files: `*.spec.ts` (unit/integration), `*.e2e.ts` (Playwright)
- `describe` blocks: class name or function name
- `it` labels: in English, behaviour-describing ("returns 400 when...")
- Always mock via `vi.mock()`, no manual stub patching
